{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "purpose": "The shared corpus for credential detection (AH-045, AH-157, AH-198). Read by the Rust detector's tests (src-tauri/harness/src/secrets.rs) and by the web app's mirror (web-app/src/lib/secretRedaction.ts). One file so the two cannot drift: a case added here fails in both suites until both detect it.",
  "rules": [
    "Every `positive` case must be detected, and the `secret` substring must not appear in redacted output.",
    "`kind` is the label the detector is expected to report. Where two rules overlap, it is the more specific one.",
    "Every `negative` case must produce no finding at all. These are the false positives that make a guard unusable: hashes, counters, placeholders and variable references.",
    "Values here are examples and non-functional. Do not add a real credential to this file."
  ],
